I experience the same problem (Angular 8.2.7): When i have a query parameter that is an array and I change the fragment by executing:
```ts
this.router.navigate(
    [],
    {
        relativeTo: this.route, // this.route: ActivatedRoute
        queryParamsHandling: 'preserve',
        fragment: 'my-fragment',
        replaceUrl: true
    }
);
```
`this.route.queryParamMap` emits an event.
